2026-11-19 The Open Kannada Authors (unreleased)
	* Added the 11 Kannada-block signs Gari lacked, drawn in its own
	stroke: U+0C80 SPACING CANDRABINDU, U+0C81 CANDRABINDU, U+0C84
	SIDDHAM, U+0CBC NUKTA, U+0CBD AVAGRAHA, U+0CE2 and U+0CE3 VOWEL SIGN
	VOCALIC L and LL, U+0CF1 JIHVAMULIYA, U+0CF2 UPADHMANIYA, and U+0964
	DANDA and U+0965 DOUBLE DANDA. Their skeletons are in
	sources/signs.json, stroked with a round pen 142 units wide (Gari's
	stem) by tools/add_signs.py. ೢ and ೣ are Gari's own ಌ and ೡ fitted to
	its subscript ಲ. The nukta is 2 dots side by side, as Kannada
	writes it.
	* Gari's substitution rules skip the nukta (a mark attachment class
	of every mark but the nukta), so a consonant with a nukta takes the
	same vowel sign and conjunct forms as without it: ಫ಼ಿ uses ಫಿ's form.
	Shaping of text without the new signs is unchanged.
	* The candrabindu moves back past the vowel signs before it, to right
	after the consonant (3 join and split passes in psts).
	* Gari's first positioning lookups, for the 2 new marks only, worked
	out from the outlines by tools/mark_offsets.py: the nukta goes under
	the consonant's body and slides aside from tails such as ಫ's, or
	drops below them; a subscript after a nukta, and the nukta under the
	hooked ು and ೂ of ಪ, ಫ and ವ, move to clear each other; the
	candrabindu goes over the consonant and rises above ಿ and ೌ, never
	past the ascent. No nukta or candrabindu overlaps other ink with any
	consonant, vowel sign or ್ರ ್ಲ ್ವ ್ಯ.
	* Unicode 15 makes jihvamuliya and upadhmaniya consonants with a
	stacker: ka or kha after jihvamuliya, and pa or pha after
	upadhmaniya, are written as subscripts. A new abvs rule (knda and
	knd2) gives them Gari's own subscript forms there, as Noto Sans
	Kannada does; it skips vowel signs, which HarfBuzz places between.
	* Structural references, for each sign's shape, size and position
	only, with no outlines copied: Noto Sans Kannada 2.006 (The Noto
	Project Authors) and Tiro Kannada 1.65 (The Indigo Project Authors),
	both under the SIL Open Font License 1.1.
	* Shaperglot now reports full kn_Knda support, so the nukta and
	avagraha exceptions are gone from CI and release/known-fails.toml.

2026-11-18 The Open Kannada Authors (1.300)
	* Ready for release. PostScript name Gari-Regular and full name Gari
	Regular, no embedding restriction (fsType 0), vendor ID NONE, and a
	copyright line without line breaks. Typo, hhea and Windows metrics
	now agree: ascent 2160 and descent 1464 with no line gap. Line height
	stays 3624 units on macOS; on Windows it grows from 3230 (typo metrics,
	used by DirectWrite and browsers) or 3400 (GDI) to the same 3624. tools/finish.py drops FontForge's
	FFTM table and the Macintosh name records, maps U+00A0 to the space,
	and writes unique glyph names. The 31 duplicate glyph names in
	Gari.sfd are renamed (glyph131.alt1 and so on), which changes no shaping. The license record holds the short OFL
	statement (the full text ships as OFL.txt), and the Navilu Reserved
	Font Name notice follows Aravinda VK's copyright line.
	* U+200C ZERO WIDTH NON-JOINER and U+200D ZERO WIDTH JOINER map to
	empty glyphs with no width.
	* tools/release.py builds TTF, OTF, WOFF2, a Kannada web subset, a
	specimen and checksums. FONTLOG.txt added.
	* Renamed COPYING to OFL.txt. Removed tools/generate_fonts.py, an
	unused GPL script from upstream, and upstream's FUNDING.yml. Added
	NOTICE.md and CONTRIBUTING.md. Scripts and tests written for this
	fork are under MIT OR Apache-2.0.
	* Renamed to Gari. Navilu is a Reserved Font Name under its SIL Open
	Font License, so a modified version cannot use it.
	* Added new-order Kannada shaping (knd2). Every lookup registered for
	knda is also registered for knd2. The below-base ligatures get knd2
	twins with virama first. For a cluster that ends in a virama, a knd2
	contextual rule gives the base its virama form and a pair adjustment
	draws the virama on the base, as old-order shaping does.
	tools/add_knd2.py makes these changes.
	* Added shaping tests (tests/test_shaping.py) and CI.
	* Added U+0CDC KANNADA ARCHAIC SHRII, U+0CDD KANNADA LETTER
	NAKAARA POLLU and U+0CF3 KANNADA SIGN COMBINING ANUSVARA ABOVE RIGHT,
	drafted with kannadi tools/glyphdraft from Gari's own stems, weight and
	anusvara. Drafts for a Kannada reader to approve.

